{"id": "EUVD-2026-47586", "enisaUuid": "3708e13c-a6c3-35b8-b3d8-11597edd9bb6", "description": "A signed integer overflow vulnerability was found in libarchive's ZIP writer. In the archive_write_zip_header function in archive_write_set_format_zip.c, when ZIP encryption is enabled and the entry file size is close to INT64_MAX, the addition of the encryption overhead to the entry size overflows int64_t, resulting in undefined behavior. This could lead to incorrect Zip64 extension decisions or potential memory corruption.", "datePublished": "2026-07-21T22:41:38", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-21T23:39:07", "baseScore": 2.9, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:L", "references": ["https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:43818", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:69553", "https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-16517", "https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2505492"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-16517", "GHSA-j8w5-8rj6-wpwf"], "assigner": "redhat", "epss": 0.08, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1902bf21-c2be-30a4-aa04-e232a240b35c", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Hardened Images", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 3.8.8-3.1.hum1"}, {"id": "6e929ca2-017d-3b86-9f7e-000a1391a852", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Enterprise Linux 10", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0:3.7.7-11.el10_2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "a6ffe782-c25f-3300-80c7-616c5e3e0a1e", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}], "isExploited": false}